 "evidence_atlas": "# Digital Rail v3 Evidence Atlas\n\n## Purpose\n\nThis atlas is a human-review aid. It identifies the strongest visual and implementation evidence in the package and separates official context, provisional derived geometry, conceptual intervention, and unresolved professional evidence.\n\n## Existing / Context Evidence\n\n- Official text scope: 43.6 km2 coordinated research area, 11.4 km2 overall design area, and 368.4 ha key detailed-design area.\n- Provisional context geometry: `geometry/site_boundary.geojson` and `geometry/key_areas.geojson`, explicitly not official redlines.\n- Public/cleared brief sources: `sources.json` records the official announcement, agent taskbook, standards and registry.\n- Context labels in the overview figure: Beijing North Station, Tsinghua Garden, Xueyuan Road, Xiaoyuehe/Vista Wing. These are orientation labels, not surveyed boundary claims.\n- Existing fabric placeholder: LU-F001 is a full-site residual retention parcel, not an existing-condition survey; do not interpret it as verified residential land use.\n\n## Proposed Intervention Evidence\n\n- `geometry/land_use.geojson`: conceptual land-use structure, full coverage, provisional.\n- `geometry/buildings.geojson`: conceptual non-overlapping building massing, not an existing-building inventory.\n- `geometry/roads.geojson`: conceptual editable roads and greenway; locked existing primary roads are not replaced.\n- `geometry/green_space.geojson` and `public_space.geojson`: conceptual blue-green/public-space network and three station squares.\n- `geometry/phasing.geojson`: P1-P3 conceptual sequence.\n- `proposal.md`: implementation cards, operator/governance/funding model, scenario capability/failure/KPI matrix, inclusive-design section and Vista Wing path.\n\n## Professional Evidence Still Missing\n\n- Official polygons, survey basemap, cadastral/ownership data, existing-building condition, traffic counts, public-service inventory, utility capacity, flood/fire/engineering evidence, statutory controls and real cost estimates.\n- Human accessibility audit and community impact assessment.\n- Human verification of rights ledger, benchmark sources, bilingual PDFs and every PDF page.\n\n## Review Rule\n\nThe package is suitable for repository intake and concept discussion. It must not be represented as an approved plan, statutory control, construction commitment, official boundary, verified baseline, or government endorsement.\n",
